	(footprint "AQROOT_Beta:Samtec_TSW-113-08-G-D-RA"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "24739bd5-275f-4f65-bf30-ee6a84bab616")
		(at 37 0 180)
		(descr "PROVISIONAL / VERIFY_BEFORE_PLACEMENT. Samtec TSW-113-08-G-D-RA, 2x13 2.54mm right-angle through-hole male header, 0.64mm square post, -G plating (10u\" gold in contact area, 3u\" gold on tail). Local Y=0 is the INSULATOR FRONT FACE. Hole rows are PARAMETRIC: row1 = B+1.50, row2 = B+4.04, generated here at B=2.54 (nominal). B = insulator depth along the board, NOT PUBLISHED by Samtec on catalog F-226 or series print Rev DS; allowed window 2.00-3.05mm. Mating post free length 5.84mm beyond the front face (published, print sht 6 note 1). Drill 1.02mm and pad 1.7mm are VERIFY: Samtec publishes 1.02+/-0.03 only for the -LL/-LA locking-lead option. The front-face SILK line is drawn at Y=+0.25 so it does not lie on Edge.Cuts; the F.Fab rectangle carries the exact front face at Y=0. Pin-1 row assignment (odd row nearest the board edge) follows KiCad convention and is VERIFY. DO NOT classify VERIFIED_VENDOR_EXACT until B and the plain -RA hole recommendation are closed.")
